# Octo — Rust development

- **Monorepo app:** `apps/router/` — Cargo package name `octo` (binary application, Rust 2021). Workspace member of the repo-root `Cargo.toml`. Entry point: `apps/router/src/main.rs`.
- **Complexity:** treat as a **simple single-crate** app inside a Cargo workspace. Prefer the single-crate guidance of [cursor-rust-rules](https://github.com/tyrchen/cursor-rust-rules) unless the user expands scope (shared libs, web frontend, CLI framework, etc.).
- **Rule set:** the general rules from [cursor-rust-rules](https://github.com/tyrchen/cursor-rust-rules) (not vendored in this repository).
- **Review bar:** `.cursor/rules/rust-pr-checklist.mdc` — per-file / per-PR checklist (types, ownership, errors, async, API, pre-commit).
- **Before finishing Rust changes:** from the monorepo root run `cargo fmt`, `cargo check -p octo`, `cargo clippy -p octo --all-targets -- -D warnings`, and `cargo test -p octo`. Run the binary from `apps/router` (or set `OCTO_CONFIG`) so `./config/` loads.
- **Errors:** prefer `Result` and `?`; avoid `unwrap()` / `expect()` outside tests or documented invariants.
- **Commit:** workspace `Cargo.lock` stays tracked (application crate).
- **Comments:** do not add comments in Rust source (`//`, `///`, `//!`, or block comments). Keep code self-explanatory; only add comments when the user explicitly requests them.
- **Module layout:** keep each `mod.rs` thin (submodules, re-exports, startup). Application settings live in **`apps/router/config/`** (split TOML files); `config.rs` merges them (optional `OCTO_CONFIG` directory or monolithic file override). Put shared application state in `state.rs`, proxy HTTP routes in `proxy/routes.rs`, and the crate-root `routes.rs` as the single app router (layers, state). Providers split into `providers/llm/` and `providers/decision/` with config wiring in `wire.rs` and vendor files (`openai.rs`, `claude.rs`, `decision/openrouter.rs`, …). Shared OpenRouter attribution and authorized POST helper in `providers/openrouter/`. Shared streaming in `providers/utils.rs`; proxy errors in `proxy/error.rs`; thin Axum entrypoints in `proxy/handler.rs`. Use traits and generic `Providers<C, M>` / `Providers<D>` so backends can be replaced via config and new enum variants without rewriting handlers.
